---
description: "Non-negotiable scheduling domain rules for the HiGHS-based scheduler"
globs: "backend/src/scheduler/**/*.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Scheduling Domain Rules

- Every shift is exactly 12 hours: DAY starts 09:00, NIGHT starts
  21:00, unless a ShiftRequirement specifies otherwise.
- Availability windows can cross midnight: if endHour <= startHour,
  the window extends into the next day. Always handle via absolute
  week-hour math (day_index*24 + hour), not string/label comparison.
- No more than `maxSeniorPerShift` (default 1) senior-level workers on
  a single shift — hard constraint, always enforced as both a `>=`
  minimum and `<=` maximum in the LP model, never just a preference.
- Fairness (even distribution across workers) is a soft objective
  (minimize max-min shift count) — never block a generation just to
  make it perfectly even.
- If the full-coverage model is infeasible, relax coverage to a
  best-effort objective and return a partial result with unfilled
  slots clearly labeled — never return nothing or fail silently.
- This is a Mixed Integer Program solved with HiGHS (npm: "highs"),
  not a CP-SAT or ML model. See scheduler.js at the repo root for the
  reference LP-formulation this module was built from — keep new
  constraints in the same style (linear sums of binary variables).
